{"fingerprint":"1350097f4124a66dae0e6e6d7c802232a1847b94d7ae79d2134438ae3edffc55","path":"src/review_gauntlet/cli.py","rule_id":"cli-contract","content":"The round-robin interleaving of stdout and stderr lines in `_agent_output_tail` does not reflect the actual temporal order of output. When an agent writes 5 lines to stdout then 3 to stderr, the tail shows them alternating (stdout[0], stderr[0], stdout[1], stderr[1], ...) rather than in emission order. Since this tail is displayed to users and persisted in activity.jsonl, it can make debugging agent failures misleading.","suggestion_code":"    entries: list[AgentOutputEntry] = [
